      "dom_id": "step-q116987",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/744485a4b00df29f1ebe3cf6789685212eb3412fac00cdb2b97170c69377f12b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's add $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/08e3cc8e56a6ade5c7da5c049cb3b6983cbb06a56c39abb10f74b9a0a192a781.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $5$ units **down**.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
