      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/72134ca14f2449f57019103d0c7e78e1c16406e7b730e7227520ae9a1273ab83.png)\n\nThe graph above shows $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+D.$ What is the value of $D?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $1.5$ units **down.**\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1.5.$ Thus, $D=-1.5.$",
