      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "What is the minimum value of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $1$ unit **up.**\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/5bf098326f9893c009df606d60f79fae788ca85a99c03562b1d2099203b62a20.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the function has no minimum value.",
